  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"terminal#8914\", \"terminal#19168\"], \"answer\": \"Reordering profiles in the Settings UI has already been requested and is tracked in terminal#8914 (terminal#19168 was closed as a duplicate of it). There is no UI for it yet. In the meantime, you can reorder profiles by editing settings.json and rearranging the entries in the `profiles.list` array; that order controls the new-tab dropdown and the ctrl+shift+number shortcuts. You can also rebind the `newTab` action with an explicit `index` to map shortcuts to whichever profile you want. The tickets do not cover reordering extension-provided entries in the dropdown, but the New Tab Menu Customization spec referenced in terminal#8914 is the related design work. Add your use case and a +1 to terminal#8914.\"}",
